// Quazi self-host compiler — design scaffold, NOT implementation.
// Component: chunks
// File: expressions.qz
// Responsibility: Coordinate translation of validated expressions into chunk instructions.
// Package boundary: Build the in-memory chunk representation from validated semantic structures; no QZI serialization, native encoding or type checking.
// TODO(P0/P1): implement existing bootstrap behavior with clean interfaces.
// Do not introduce new language features before bootstrap parity.
// Split boundary: this file remains the coordinator for its responsibility;
// implementation details belong to the adjacent modules listed below.
//   expression/calls.qz: Lower direct/indirect, method, intrinsic and foreign calls into QZI.
//   expression/operators.qz: Lower arithmetic, comparison, bitwise, cast and logical operations into QZI.
//   expression/aggregates.qz: Lower struct/enum/array construction and aggregate field access into QZI.
//   expression/places.qz: Lower lvalue/place addressing, indexing, loads, stores and assignments into QZI.
